Subject: [PATCH] bpf: support getsockopt in UDP sendmsg hooks

Allow Samsung's network socket accounting program to read socket options at
the IPv4 and IPv6 sendmsg hooks, as in upstream Linux v5.15. Both use the
existing sock_addr getsockopt implementation and argument validation.

--- a/net/core/filter.c
+++ b/net/core/filter.c
@@ -7113,6 +7113,8 @@
 		switch (prog->expected_attach_type) {
 		case BPF_CGROUP_INET4_CONNECT:
 		case BPF_CGROUP_INET6_CONNECT:
+		case BPF_CGROUP_UDP4_SENDMSG:
+		case BPF_CGROUP_UDP6_SENDMSG:
 			return &bpf_sock_addr_getsockopt_proto;
 		default:
 			return NULL;
